      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Reviewed on OpenReview: https: // openreview. net/ forum? id= pvtgffHtJm",
      "bbox": [
        71.99996948242188,
        428.1983947753906,
        407.693359375,
        436.4654235839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Abstract",
      "bbox": [
        282.6249694824219,
        467.1249694824219,
        329.36981201171875,
        477.7411804199219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We propose Diffusion Model Predictive Control (D-MPC), a novel MPC approach that",
      "bbox": [
        107.35700225830078,
        499.3019104003906,
        504.5533752441406,
        509.2645263671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "learns a multi-step action proposal and a multi-step dynamics model, both using diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        107.86499786376953,
        511.2579345703125,
        504.2967529296875,
        521.2205200195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "models, and combines them for use in online MPC. On the popular D4RL benchmark, we",
      "bbox": [
        107.86499786376953,
        523.212890625,
        504.305419921875,
        533.1754760742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "show performance that is significantly better than existing model-based offline planning",
      "bbox": [
        107.86499786376953,
        535.1679077148438,
        504.3197326660156,
        545.1304931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "methods using MPC (e.g. MBOP(Argenson & Dulac-Arnold, 2021)) and competitive with",
      "bbox": [
        107.86499786376953,
        547.1229248046875,
        504.2763671875,
        557.0855102539062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "state-of-the-art (SOTA) model-based and model-free reinforcement learning methods. We",
      "bbox": [
        107.86499786376953,
        559.077880859375,
        504.3009033203125,
        569.0404663085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "additionally illustrate D-MPC’s ability to optimize novel reward functions at run time and",
      "bbox": [
        107.86499786376953,
        571.0328979492188,
        504.3013916015625,
        580.9954833984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "adapt to novel dynamics, and highlight its advantages compared to existing diffusion-based",
      "bbox": [
        107.86499786376953,
        582.9888916015625,
        504.30706787109375,
        592.9514770507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "planning baselines.",
      "bbox": [
        107.86499786376953,
        594.9439086914062,
        189.94686889648438,
        604.906494140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        637.31005859375,
        78.57536315917969,
        647.9263305664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "bbox": [
        91.72608184814453,
        637.31005859375,
        159.0458221435547,
        647.9263305664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Model predictive control (MPC), also called receding horizon control, uses a dynamics model and an action",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        663.4539184570312,
        540.230712890625,
        673.41650390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "selection mechanism (planner) to construct “agents” that can solve a wide variety of tasks by means of",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        675.408935546875,
        540.20751953125,
        685.3715209960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "maximizing a known objective function (see e.g., Schwenzer et al. (2021) for a review of MPC). More precisely,",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        687.3638916015625,
        541.5975341796875,
        697.3264770507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we want to design an agent that maximizes an objective function J(at:t+F −1, st+1:t+F ) over a planning horizon",
      "bbox": [
        71.64099884033203,
        699.3189086914062,
        540.0482788085938,
        710.7764892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "∗Corresponding author: stannis@google.com",
      "bbox": [
        82.9260025024414,
        722.5657958984375,
        247.7608184814453,
        731.4559936523438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
